## SOURCE
def first_value():String
  print("first-call\n")
  return "A"
end
def second_value():String
  print("second-call\n")
  return "B"
end
def third_value():String
  print("third-call\n")
  return "C"
end
def wrap(value:String):String
  print("wrap-call\n")
  return "<#{value}>"
end
def main()
  print("[#{first_value()}|#{wrap("middle #{second_value()} #{ "deep #{third_value()}" }")}|end]\n")
end
## EXPECTED APPLICATION STDOUT
first-call
second-call
third-call
wrap-call
[A|<middle B deep C>|end]

## NOTE
Canonical EX-012 coverage for recursive exact-String interpolation, a nested direct-call argument, three recursive levels, once-only source order with the inner argument complete before wrap, existing String composition, and no conversion.
